# A sketchy landing is a miss. Rosa sets an Impossible at the mark (her clock starts after the 2 s
# pause; she rides the lane, pops on the mark and lands it). Your try: the same Impossible, landed
# 26 degrees off the line of travel (the bot lands it crooked on purpose): sketchy, not clean, so
# the match fails and you get an S; then it is your set (the setter changes every round).
park soma
cmd 0 run skate rosa
bot skate sketchy
run 1300
expect event skateTurn{who=local,role=set,seconds=25} within 1..1
expect event npcTrick{trick=Impossible} within 520..535
expect event skateSet{by=local,trick=impossible,name=Impossible} within 596..604
expect event skateTurn{who=player,role=match,trick=impossible,name=Impossible} within 596..604
expect event pop within 1048..1058
expect event trickEnd{trick=Impossible} within 1100..1115
expect event land{quality=sketchy} within 1165..1173
expect event skateMatch{by=player,ok=false,trick=impossible,got=impossible,reason=sketchy,line=That's a letter.} within 1165..1173
expect event skateLetter{who=player,letters=S} within 1165..1173
expect event skateTurn{who=player,role=set} within 1165..1173
expect no event bail
expect session.skatePlayer == S at end
expect event skateLetter{who=local} count == 0
